NAME
       install - copy files and set their attributes

SYNOPSIS
       install [-cCDpsTv] [-m MODE] [-o OWNER] [-g GROUP] SRC
          DEST install [...] SRC... DIR  |  install [...] -t
          DIR SRC...  |  install -d [...] DIR...

DESCRIPTION
       Copy files and set their mode (default 0755), owner and
       group. -D creates the leading directories of DEST, -d
       creates directories, -p keeps the times, -C leaves an
       identical destination alone, -s is accepted and does
       nothing (there is no strip for WebAssembly). If the
       kernel cannot set modes or owners (ENOSYS), install
       says so once and carries on.

NOTES
       -s is accepted and does nothing (there is no strip for
       WebAssembly). Where the kernel cannot change modes or
       owners yet, install warns once and goes on.

SEE ALSO
       sh(1)

